          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em monoid axiom
            is an extra condition on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            that helps to make its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} model structure on monoids in a monoidal model category
            exist and be well behaved.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #MonoidAxiom.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              We say a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              satisfies the
              %strong monoid axiom
              if every morphism that is obtained as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
              of acyclic cofibrations with any object is a weak equivalence.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> Schwede-Shipley 00, def. 3.3.
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In particular, the axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidAxiom"}
              says that for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes (-)
              sends acyclic cofibrations to weak equivalences.
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"}> cofibrantly generated model category
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"}> symmetric monoidal category
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"}> monoidal model category
                  \.
            %p Then if the monoid axiom holds for the set of generating acyclic cofibrations it holds for all acyclic cofibrations.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> Schwede-Shipley 00, lemma 3.5
            ).
          #ExistenceOfModelstructureOnMonoids.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              satisfies the monoid axiom and
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              %li
                %p
                  all objects are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+objects"} small objects
            %p
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi F
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \dashv U) : Mon(C) \stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}} C
              exists on its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              and hence provides a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} model structure on monoids
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> Schwede-Shipley 00, theorem 4.1
            )
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Monoidal model categories that satisfy the monoid axiom (as well as the other conditions sufficient for the
              %a{:href => "#ExistenceOfModelstructureOnMonoids"} above theorem
              on the existence of transferred model structures on categories of monoids) include
            %p
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %ul
              %li
                the standard
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %p
              with respect to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            %ul
              %li
                the projective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
                for connective chanin complexes with fibrations the surjections in positive degree
            %p
              and with respect to a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+Gamma-spaces"} model structure on Gamma-spaces
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> Schwede-Shipley 00, section 5
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MMSS00"} MMSS 00, theorem 12.1 (iii)
